@startuml example-domain-adaptation
' Domain adaptation as a two-expert mixture whose weight λ is fitted on a held-out
' in-domain development set, then reported on a disjoint test set. Colour: corpora
' (grey), general expert (blue), domain expert (green), mixture (steel blue),
' the tuning search (purple), the report (teal).
' Render: plantuml -tsvg docs/diagrams/example-domain-adaptation.puml
' Source of truth for Figure 1 in docs/examples/domain-adaptation.md §3
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam rectangle {
  FontColor white
  FontStyle bold
  BorderColor #263238
  roundCorner 12
}
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam ArrowFontColor #37474F
title Domain adaptation — mixture of two experts, λ fitted on a held-out dev set

rectangle "**general corpus**\nbroad · large · out-of-domain" as gc #546E7A
rectangle "**domain corpus**\nnarrow · small · in-domain" as dc #546E7A

rectangle "**ℙ_g — general expert**\nTrainerBuilder.order(n).train(reader)\nwide coverage, wrong priors" as g #1565C0
rectangle "**ℙ_d — domain expert**\nsame order · same tokenizer\nright priors, sparse & narrow" as d #2E7D32

rectangle "**mixture**\nℙ_λ(w | h) = (1−λ)·ℙ_g(w | h) + λ·ℙ_d(w | h)\nλ = 0 ⇒ general · λ = 1 ⇒ domain" as mix #1B6CA8

rectangle "**dev set**\nheld out · in-domain" as dev #546E7A
rectangle "**fit λ**\nLL(λ) = Σ log ℙ_λ is **concave** (Lemma 1)\n⇒ grid / ternary search or EM finds\nthe **global** optimum λ*" as tune #6A1B9A

rectangle "**test set**\nheld out · in-domain · disjoint from dev" as test #546E7A
rectangle "**report**\nPP_general vs PP_domain vs PP(λ*)\nOOV coverage · per-word scores" as rep #00838F

gc --> g
dc --> d
g --> mix : ℙ_g
d --> mix : ℙ_d
dev --> tune
mix --> tune : evaluate PP_dev(λ)
tune --> mix : λ ← λ* = argmin PP_dev(λ)
mix --> rep : score with λ*
test --> rep
g --> rep : baseline
d --> rep : baseline

note right of tune #F3E5F5
  PP is monotone-decreasing in LL,
  so **min PP ≡ max LL**. Any local
  optimum of a concave objective on
  [0, 1] is the global one — a coarse
  grid followed by a ternary search
  is sufficient and safe.
end note

note bottom of d #E8F5E9
  Small domain corpus? Lower its order
  (sparser data) and lean toward ℙ_g;
  embeddings can instead be **fine-tuned**
  with EmbeddingTrainer::train_continued.
end note

@enduml
